    "id": "rk_a6703ce4b19fcd511ee2",
    "text": "One argument from silence worth knowing, from the other direction: <cite index=\"30-1\">no form of the Testimonium is cited by Justin Martyr, Theophilus, Melito, Minucius Felix, Irenaeus, Clement of Alexandria, Julius Africanus, Tertullian, Hippolytus, Origen, Methodius, or Lactantius — all of whom show familiarity with Josephus.</cite> The counter-explanation is also worth knowing: <cite index=\"30-1\">if the original text did nothing more than establish that Jesus existed, and nobody in the first centuries questioned that, there would be no occasion to quote it.</cite>",
